# The Shadower's second class node: a barrage that is held, not pressed, with
# the dagger landing fifteen times in a second and a half.
#
# GMS's own figures: 660+27x% seven times on eight enemies, fifteen attacks
# 100ms apart, all ignoring defense completely.
#
# The count is the one number the client states twice and contradicts itself on:
# `updatableTime 2000` over `attackDelay 100` gives twenty, and `x` gives
# fifteen. Fifteen is right, as the cooldown refund shows: GMS refunds 3.3
# seconds per unused attack, so at twenty a cast cancelled after one attack
# would refund 62.7 seconds of a 60-second cooldown and make Sonic Blow free
# forever. At fifteen it leaves 13.8 seconds, the loop the skill is built
# around.
#
# A hold, so 600ms is the minimum: 240ms of wind-up and a 360ms release, all
# positive frames and so scaled by attack speed. The 100ms beat is the skill's
# own. It always runs to its last attack: a hold normally stops once the crowd
# in front of it is dead, but this one doesn't end on a strike, and GMS's reason
# to release early is the cooldown refund, which isn't modelled here.
#
# Dropped: the 1000 MP, the knockback and status immunity while it runs, the
# cancel into Trickblade or Shadow Assault, and the refund for releasing early.
# The last three all need a button this game doesn't have.
name: "Sonic Blow"
description:
  "Move faster than the speed of sound, dealing consecutive attacks along the "
  "way. You take less damage for as long as the attack runs."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ATTACK
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_SHADOWER_V skill_order: 2 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_JOB
max_level: 30
required_equip_type: EQUIP_TYPE_DAGGER
base_delay_ms: 600
cooldown_seconds: 60.0
max_enemies: 8
lines: 7
base {
  skill_pct: 6.87
  ied_pct: 1.00
}
per_level { skill_pct: 0.27 }
channel {
  pulse_interval_ms: 100
  max_pulses: 15
  finish_delay_ms: 360
  damage_taken_pct: 0.50
}
